# IMPORT MERGING (-I): the root document imports imported.ttl, and both use
# blank nodes. Each parse numbers its blank nodes from 0, so the CLI must
# standardize the documents apart (an offset on the import's ids) or the
# two restrictions below would collide. Pinned by `golden` with
#   howl validate root.ttl -I imported.ttl --report
# Expect: A subClassOf C, through the root's A ⊑ ∃r.B and the import's
# ∃r.B ⊑ C; the import's anonymous-individual assertion is an omission
# whose text shows its (offset) blank id.
@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

<http://example.org/root> a owl:Ontology ; owl:imports <http://example.org/imported> .
:r a owl:ObjectProperty .
:A a owl:Class . :B a owl:Class .
:A rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :r ; owl:someValuesFrom :B ] .
